-- Ekwo OS — Nepal: chart of accounts, journals, taxes and defaults.
--
-- Generated from packs/np at version 0.1.0, do not edit.
-- Change the pack and run `ekwo pack build np`; `ekwo pack check --all`
-- refuses a seed that is not the exact output of its pack, and the CI runs it.
--
-- Community pack — not reviewed.
-- Written from:
--   Value-Added Tax Act, 2052 (1996), English text as amended up to the Financial Act, 2021 (2078) — s. 5 (the charge, and the exemption of Schedule 1 with the loss of the deduction), s. 6 (the time of supply), s. 7 (the rate of thirteen percent, zero rate for Schedule 2), s. 8(2) (a service acquired from outside Nepal), s. 10 (registration), s. 14 and 14A (invoice and electronic invoice), s. 17 (tax deduction), s. 18 (monthly return within twenty-five days), s. 19 (payment within twenty-five days). The Schedules are not part of the file that could be read (Inland Revenue Department of Nepal (copy kept by the Internet Archive; the Department's own link no longer answers))
--     https://web.archive.org/web/2023id_/https://www.ird.gov.np/public/pdf/1140227555.pdf
--   Value Added Tax Act, 2052, as amended up to the Economic Act, 2082 — the Department's page for the current consolidated text, in Nepali; its PDF could not be downloaded from the machine this pack was written on, so the amendments since the Financial Act, 2021 are a gap recorded in the README (Inland Revenue Department of Nepal)
--     https://ird.gov.np/content/13407/value-added-tax-act--2052--as-amended/
--   Nepal — use of IFRS Standards by jurisdiction: the Nepal Financial Reporting Standards 2024 for public-interest entities, the NFRS for SMEs mandatory for SMEs without public accountability from 16 July 2024, the NAS for Micro Entities, issued by the Accounting Standards Board Nepal; the Companies Act requires financial statements to follow the accounting standards in force (IFRS Foundation)
--     https://www.ifrs.org/use-around-the-world/use-of-ifrs-standards-by-jurisdiction/view-jurisdiction/nepal/
--   Income Tax Act, 2058 (2002), unofficial translation — the income year, from the first day of Shrawan (tentatively 15 July) to the last day of Ashad (tentatively 14 July) of the next year; read through a search extract, the file itself did not download whole (Inland Revenue Department of Nepal)
--     https://www.ird.gov.np/public/pdf/379988550.pdf
--   Inland Revenue Department of Nepal — the Department's site, where the Acts, notices and the taxpayer services are published; returns are filed electronically through its taxpayer portal (Inland Revenue Department of Nepal)
--     https://ird.gov.np/
--
-- Reference data: `install_country_template()` copies it into a company,
-- nothing here belongs to a company.

